# Sprout(A) (PLDI 2026 artifact, Zenodo record 19600644) Table 1 protocols, in the order of the artifact's
# verify_all.sh: the file under benchmarks/sprouta/examples/sprout/, its Table 1 row name and |P| (both from
# examples/table1_empty.txt of the image), and the expected implementability per network -- p2p (p2pbox),
# sb (senderbox), mb (mailbox), monob (monobox), bag -- as Y, N or ? (not known to this tree), then the source:
#   paper:table1  Table 1 of the paper, Li and Wies, "Implementability of Global Distributed Protocols modulo
#                 Network Architectures", arXiv 2602.10320 v1 (read 2026-10-23); its marks are Sprout(A)'s
#                 results, which the paper states were checked consistent with SPROUT's CAV 2025 p2p results,
#                 with Lemma 7.9's relations between architectures, and by manual inspection (Section 7.1).
#                 A ? there is an inconclusive run (a timeout), not a ground truth, and stays ? here, except
#   p2p:cav25     where the p2p column is ? in the paper and SPROUT's CAV 2025 Table 2 gives the answer
#                 (fwd-auth-no N, higher-lower-winning Y; script/fetch/sprout.expected).
# The artifact README's sample rows disagree with the paper on HigherLower under mb and monob (README Y, paper N);
# the paper is followed. The artifact carries no ground-truth column: table1_empty.txt has only names and |P|.
# travel-agency is listed with |P| = 2 although its file has three participants (as in CAV 2025's Table 2).
# Columns are separated by one TAB.
